  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington is running hot and Hicksville is showing operational stress\u2014one structural and one that needs your attention.\n\nPort Washington delivered a strong week: yesterday's $3,298 revenue on six groomers ($484/groomer) sits 4% below the 30-day baseline, but that's noise\u2014the real story is transaction velocity (up 19%) and core groom revenue up 16% week-over-week. Month-to-date you're at $25,778 versus a DOW-adjusted expectation of $26,491, a real miss of 2.7%, not calendar. The concern: add-on attach collapsed from 48% to 32%, and retail dropped 10%. This is a front-of-house discipline issue, not demand. You should be proud of year-to-date momentum\u2014you're up 53% in revenue and 54% in appointments against last year. Inventory pressure is real (three best-selling treats completely out), so reorder those three items today.\n\nHicksville is underperforming. Month-to-date revenue is down 17% despite a favorable calendar (+1.4% DOW-adjusted), which means this is operational. Yesterday's $886 came from only two groomers at $342 each, 8% below the 30-day baseline of $370. Worse: add-on revenue went to zero (was 60% attach last week), and retail is down 17%. The leading indicator flashing red is visit-cadence drift\u2014your 12+ week dormancy bucket grew 1.8 points, signaling stealth churn. You have 58 customers at risk with $40k annual value. Bather coverage is zero; consider whether that's constraining groomer throughput.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Port Washington today 6 groomers + 7.0h bathers, tomorrow 5 groomers + 7.0h bathers; Hicksville today 2 groomers + 0h bathers, tomorrow 2 groomers + 0h bathers; next 7 days 40 groomer-days across both locations (29 Port, 11 Hicksville) with 43h bathers all at Port.**"
